from __future__ import annotations

"""Public-release helpers for the sliding-window ISC analyses.

Participant identifiers are not embedded in this file. The release supports two
participant-dependence designs:

1) ``independent_modalities``: neural and behavioral participants are resampled
   independently, while matching IDs preserve repeated participants
   across datasets within each modality.
2) ``matched_modalities``: one matching-ID list is shared across neural
   and behavioral modalities and receives one common bootstrap count vector.

For exact reproduction, provide local matching-ID configuration and a
Stage-2 mixed-model design table. The latter supplies the information
needed for crossed-participant random intercepts, repeated-dyad random
intercepts, and stimulus/dataset fixed effects. Keep both outside the public
repository or list them in ``.gitignore``.

Acknowledgement
---------------
Parts of this ISC implementation were developed with substantial reference to
the Naturalistic Data Analysis tutorials:
https://naturalistic-data.org/content/intro.html
We gratefully acknowledge the authors and contributors of that resource.

Methodological reference
-----------------------
Chen, G., Taylor, P. A., Shin, Y. W., Reynolds, R. C., & Cox, R. W. Untangling the relatedness among correlations, Part II: Inter-subject correlation group analysis through linear mixed-effects modeling. NeuroImage 147, 825-840 (2017).
"""

